Using the `\result` variable is not sufficient here because the postcondition depends on the input `o` and the state after removal. We are only allowed to use publicly accessible observer methods, and `contains` is one such method.

Thus, the correct assertion is that after the operation, the set does not contain `o`.

<code>assert !this.contains(o);</code>
